                        ],
                        "form": "doolies"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d5c8d78c-5a2a-30b3-aa10-75ee397ee276",
                        "entry_id": "9c5fcc90-1a45-36c4-b602-b3ff2e099daf",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A basic Indian litter or sedan chair made of poles, ropes, and a seat or cloth."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "India",
                            "historical"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "81576ee7-3574-47b2-bf0d-cb86805a7ff9",
                                "sense_id": "d5c8d78c-5a2a-30b3-aa10-75ee397ee276",
                                "text": "The dhulí is a slight bamboo framework covered with coarse cloth, about two and a half feet square, with a bedding made of string woven across, on which the passenger sits. It is slung on a stout bamboo pole, and carried by two or four men."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "de254293-c7fa-4e34-aed0-a8e1be1c35f4",
                                "sense_id": "d5c8d78c-5a2a-30b3-aa10-75ee397ee276",
                                "text": "He said I should not be able to ride much farther, as the pass beyond Sultanpoor was utterly impracticable for horses; coolies, however, awaited me with a dooly, one of those low litters slung on a bamboo, in which you may travel swiftly and without effort, but to the destruction of the digestive organs."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e36ce849-0c50-439e-ba33-7e11a19a0e3d",
                                "sense_id": "d5c8d78c-5a2a-30b3-aa10-75ee397ee276",
                                "text": "“Not going out this journey,” gasped Bobby, as he was lifted from the doolie. “Not going out this journey.”"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1e54c47a-1487-34ec-abca-3e72347e1121",
                        "entry_id": "9c5fcc90-1a45-36c4-b602-b3ff2e099daf",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Synonym of stretcher, a basic litter used for transport of the ill and injured."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "India",
                            "archaic"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "608b23b3-aeb3-499f-8e26-acab0885f2a4",
                                "sense_id": "1e54c47a-1487-34ec-abca-3e72347e1121",
                                "text": "He also, in conjunction with Private John Ryan, rushed into the street under a heavy fire, and took Captain Arnold, 1st Madras Fusiliers, out of a dooly, and brought him into the house, that officer being again hit while they were so doing."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f0f39e30-30d4-442d-8d57-7e953833159d",
                                "sense_id": "1e54c47a-1487-34ec-abca-3e72347e1121",
                                "text": "I thought at first I was as good as done for; however, on regaining a little strength, I looked around, and seeing none of our men in the place, and thinking it more than probable, from what I knew of their character, that the very men whom I had been endeavouring to save might take it into their heads to give me the \"coup de grace\" now I was left alone, I made a desperate effort, got on my legs, and managed to hobble out, when I soon found some of our men, who supported me until a dooly could be brought, into which I was placed, and was soon on my way to the doctor."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
